model.en:
Extract one method per responsibility and let importCsv read as a narrative:<br/><pre>async function importCsv(file: File) {
  const rows = parseRows(file);
  const { valid, rejected } = validateRows(rows);
  const fresh = await dedupe(valid);
  const inserted = await insertValid(fresh);
  return reportRejected(inserted, rejected);
}</pre>Five lines, each a domain responsibility. <code>parseRows</code>, <code>validateRows</code>, <code>dedupe</code>, <code>insertValid</code>, <code>reportRejected</code> are seams; you do <em>not</em> extract <code>rows.push(r)</code> or a single <code>db.query</code> call into their own methods — those are one-liners, not responsibilities, and extracting them would be the shattering failure mode. A change to the dedup rule now lives only in <code>dedupe</code>; the rest is untouched.

